  "details": "Hi, I've been a pretty avid supporter of getting this into the game for a very long while now. Ever since the avatars 3.0 beta when users found out we could change scale, A lot of us have wanted this quite a lot, but the ability was taken away as soon as 3.0 actually released. A lot of us were really mad as that seemed like a non issue to take away. Anyways the community eventually came out with a mod for this scaling stuff and it was by far the best implementation of scaling we've had yet. It supported us scaling quickly or slowly, in increments or however we wanted to do it. It felt good, natural, and it just worked. Obviously we can't use mods anymore so that method got taken away from us as well. So we all became content using this workaround method we've been using for a while now utilizing that OSC reset. While yeah this works and we can change to any scale we want to, it's janky and takes a lot of unnecessary time.\n\nNow today i'm told that avatar scaling was implemented officially, but with very hard capped limits for some reason? And it's still not as good or natural feeling as the old modded scaling felt, but honestly that's fine. I am glad that we finally get it back but I just can't understand why we can't have it work the way we want to, and why there's limits being placed on it. If people want to be microscopic they'll just upload an avatar that small, if they want to be gargantuan then they'll just upload an avatar that big. I'm not sure if we're being given limits to try and stop people from being annoying, or to stop cheating in some maps like some have said, but if people want to be annoying, they have plenty of other ways to do so than just being big. Besides, back when the scale mod was going around, tons of users were having fun experimenting with things but as soon as the novelty wore off, things were just fine, no issues.\n\nThe only thing I can imagine is that some issues arise, or edge case problems at extreme ends of the spectrum, this i know to be true as once you get really big, its harder to interact with the menu. But that's fine, I think the users that do that sort of thing kind of expect there to be an issue and we already know about it.\n\nI'm glad that we have the scaler now at least, it will help prevent a TON of people from having to upload tons of different avatars just for different sizes, which is good on performance and for my sanity. But I just wish it was done differently, and more like how the scaling worked back with the mod we had. There aren't a lot of us users that will realistically need to go beyond 5M tall, but for us that do occasionally, having all these limits and workarounds really sucks.\n\nTL:DR- Thank you to the devs that worked on implementing this, it's a great improvement and will save a ton of people a ton of time, not having to have multiple uploads for the same avatar is nice. However, It would be great if we had some dynamic scaling capabilities. I'm not an expert but i believe what I'm asking for is for live/dynamic adjustment of our avatar height and IPD. Essentially to act exactly how the scaling worked when the scalegoesbrrr mod was a thing.",
